      "id": "gr.b2.reported-speech-advanced",
      "cefr": "B2",
      "title": "Reported speech: time, place and viewpoint shifts",
      "objective": "Adjust deictic words and viewpoint beyond simple tense backshift.",
      "concept": {
        "en": "Advanced reported speech allows selective backshift, changes in modal meaning, and preservation of a tense when the information remains true or the time relationship is already clear.",
        "vi": "Tường thuật nâng cao cho phép lùi thì có chọn lọc, thay đổi modal và giữ nguyên thì khi thông tin vẫn đúng hoặc quan hệ thời gian đã rõ."
      },
      "formulae": [
        "backshift when viewpoint moves back",
        "no compulsory backshift for still-true/current information"
      ],
      "whenToUse": [
        "Report speech naturally rather than applying mechanical tense changes in every context."
      ],
      "forms": {
        "positive": [
          "The teacher said that water boils at 100°C.",
          "Mina said she'd finished the work the day before.",
          "He told me he might be late."
